# ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Conventional Commits Template
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# <type>(<scope>): <subject>          ← REQUIRED (≤50 chars)
#
# <body>                               ← OPTIONAL (wrap at 72 chars)
#
# <footer>                             ← OPTIONAL
#   Co-authored-by: aetheris <agents.aetheris@gmail.com>
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Types:
#   feat      New feature
#   fix       Bug fix
#   docs      Documentation only
#   style     Formatting (no logic change)
#   refactor  Neither fix nor feature
#   perf      Performance improvement
#   test      Adding/fixing tests
#   build     Build system or dependencies
#   ci        CI/CD configuration
#   chore     Other (no src/test change)
#   revert    Reverts a previous commit
#
# Rules:
#   - Subject: imperative mood ("add" not "added")
#   - Subject: no period at end
#   - Subject: ≤50 characters
#   - Body: explain WHAT and WHY, not HOW
#   - Footer: reference issues (Closes #123) and/or Co-authored-by trailer
#   - Breaking: add ! after type (feat!:) or
#     BREAKING CHANGE: in footer
#
# Examples:
#   feat(auth): add OAuth2 Google login
#
#   Implement secure OAuth2 token exchange with PKCE support.
#
#   Co-authored-by: aetheris <agents.aetheris@gmail.com>
#
